  "query_preview": "..After a weak trough passed by yesterday, we will \nremain in a quiet weather pattern through the rest of the week. \nOverall expect gradually warming temperatures, generally light \nwinds, and fully dry conditions each day through Saturday. A weak \ndisturbance will dive southward along the California coast into \nthe Baja peninsula on Wednesday, but this will bring minimal \nimpacts save for some high clouds. Ridging continues to build \nthereafter into the weekend, with temperatures eventually peaking \nat 5-10 degrees above normal on Friday-Saturday. Expect pleasant \nweather for Thanksgiving!\n\nThe ridge begins to flatten early next week, and we may see a trough \nbrush past northern Arizona on Sunday-Monday. However the ensemble \nconsensus is for conditions to remain mostly dry. A potentially more \nimpactful trough may be on the horizon by next Tuesday, stay tuned \nfor updates on this period.",
